course: dictionary
lesson: 10375
title: Treasury: money, treasure and collections
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A treasury is a place where money or treasure is kept. In a story, a castle's treasury might hold gold coins and jewels. In the game example, «Spain fills its treasury from American silver mines» means Spain keeps the silver it gets from those mines in a safe place.
explain: Treasury can also be a name with a capital T: «the Treasury». This is a government department that looks after a country's money, taxes and spending. When you see «the Treasury» in the news, it is about government money, not a box of gold.
explain: Treasury can mean a big collection of valuable things, too. «A treasury of fairy tales» is a book or set of many good stories. Read the words around the word to choose the right meaning: money, a department, or a collection.
fact: A treasury is a place where treasure or money is kept.
fact: «The Treasury» with a capital T is a government department that manages a country's money, taxes and spending.
fact: «A treasury of» means a rich collection of valuable things, such as stories or poems.
fact: In the game Europa Universalis, «Spain fills its treasury from American silver mines».
fact: Clue words like taxes, spending and government point to the department meaning; words like gold and castle point to the storeroom meaning.
exercise: «Spain fills its treasury from American silver mines.» What is a treasury here? | A long, quiet walk | A type of ship | *A place where money or treasure is kept | A kind of mine for digging up coal
exercise: «The Treasury decides how much money the country can spend on schools.» Which job does the Treasury do? | Teaches children in a school | *Manages a country's money, taxes and spending | Sells fairy tale books | Builds castles on hills
exercise: Mia reads «a treasury of fairy tales». What does this mean? | A government office for taxes | A fairy who counts money | Gold coins hidden under a bed | *A rich collection of fairy tales
test: «The royal treasury was full of gold coins.» What does treasury mean? | A soft blanket | A small boat | A type of tree | *A place where money or treasure is kept
test: In news about a country, «the Treasury» is which of these? | A type of weather | Lunch in the school hall | A kind of castle | *The government department that manages money, taxes and spending
exam: Which sentence uses treasury to mean a big collection of good things? | «The king locked his gold in the treasury.» | *«She read a treasury of poems before bed.» | «The mine was dark and deep.» | «The Treasury decides how much the government spends.»
